{
 "about": "Every OBP-API call the scripts make: verb, path (OBP placeholders in capitals), the source file, the text that makes the call (needles) and the response fields the scripts read. The paths of entities and their records follow OBP_ENTITY_SPACE_ID: at system level they are .../system-dynamic-entities and /obp/dynamic-entity/ENTITY, in a bank they are .../banks/BANK_ID/dynamic-entities and /obp/dynamic-entity/banks/BANK_ID/ENTITY, and each call is listed once with the paths of both where it can use either. A call through obp_space.management_path or record_path is listed with the paths that function builds. The reads are kept by hand. obp-api-contract/snapshot.json is what an OBP-API documents for these calls, written by obp-api-contract/snapshot.py. tests/test_obp_api_contract.py checks this list against the source and the snapshot.",
 "version_policy": "Each call writes the OBP-API version it needs in its own path. One configured version cannot serve them all, because an endpoint exists only in the versions OBP-API documents it for. tests/test_obp_api_contract.py checks every call against the endpoint documented for the version it names, and tests/test_obp_api_version.py fails on any version below v5.1.0 in the scripts and the documents. To move a call to a newer version, change its path and run snapshot.py again.",
